module

public import StacksFrontier.CategoryTheory.Sites.Cohomology.Perfect.LeftDualLocalRetractOnASite
public import StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.SliceRestrictionTensoratorSections
public import StacksFrontier.Homology.DerivedCategory.Monoidal.MapDerivedCategoryMonoidalOnModels
public import StacksFrontier.CategoryTheory.Sites.Cohomology.CompactObjects.ExtensionByZeroUnitAtTerminal

/-!
# The retract of Stacks 0FPV on a slice, along a subcomplex of the slice

Let `(C, O)` be a ringed site and let `N` be a left dual of `M` in the monoidal category `D(O)` of
Stacks 0FPT. The proof of Stacks 0FPV writes the coevaluation, on the members `W` of a covering,
as a finite sum `η(1) = ∑ᵢ fᵢ ⊗ gᵢ` against K-flat representatives `M^•`, `N^•`, and then
*replaces `C` by `C/W`*: the sections `fᵢ` become sections over the final object of the slice,
and `M|_W` is a direct summand of every subcomplex of `M^•|_W` containing them. This file proves
that statement with the subcomplex taken **on the slice**, which is what lets it be generated by
finitely many sections over the final object.

## Main results

* `CategoryTheory.ExactPairing.exists_section_of_map_coevaluation_factors`: a factorization of
  the image coevaluation under a monoidal functor exhibits a retract.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.mu_restriction_ιTensorObj_unit_tmul`: the tensorator of
  restriction of complexes to a slice carries a local pure tensor to the local pure tensor.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.restriction_coevaluation_eq`: the coevaluation of the restricted
  pairing, through the restricted representatives.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.exists_section_restriction_of_sliceSection`: the direct-summand
  step along a subcomplex of the slice.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.exists_presieve_sliceRetract`: **the local retract of Stacks
  0FPV along subcomplexes of the slices.**

## Implementation notes

The restricted pairing is `CategoryTheory.ExactPairing.map` along the strong monoidal structure
`Stacks.Cohomology.DerivedRestriction.mapDerivedCategoryMonoidal` of derived restriction, whose
tensorator is obtained by localization and is given by no formula. Its value at two K-flat
complexes is computed by `CategoryTheory.Functor.mapDerivedCategoryMonoidal_μ_Q` in terms
of the tensorator of restriction of complexes, and that one is computed on local pure tensors by
`Stacks.SliceRestrictionTensorSections.mu_overFunctorMonoidal_shSec_tmul`. With both in hand the
coevaluation of the restricted pairing is the morphism attached to the restricted section, read
through the K-flat comparison of the slice.

Several steps are taken as terms of abstract composition lemmas: the module categories of the
slice have two spellings, `SheafOfModules ((ringSheaf O).over W)` and
`SheafOfModules (ringSheaf (O.over W))`, which agree by `rfl` but not for the rewriting tactics.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0FPV](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0FPV)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0FPT](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0FPT)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

